 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "There is: há",
     "texto": [
      "Unlike English «there is» and «there are», **há** never changes: **Há uma mesa** (there is a table), **há três quartos** (there are three bedrooms).",
      "Negative: **não há**. Question: **Há jardim?**",
      "It is pronounced like the article «a», but it is spelled with an «h» and an accent."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The parts of the house",
     "texto": [
      "Be careful with these words: **o quarto** is «the bedroom», **a sala** is «the living room» and the bathroom is **a casa de banho**.",
      "**A cozinha** (the kitchen), **a varanda** (the balcony), **o jardim** (the garden). A flat is **um apartamento**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Furniture",
     "texto": [
      "**A cama**, **o sofá**, **o armário**, **a televisão**. The window is **a janela** and the door is **a porta**. The fridge is **o frigorífico**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "My and your, with no article in front",
     "texto": [
      "After a contraction such as «no» or «da», the possessive goes without repeating the article: **no meu quarto** (in my bedroom), **na minha casa** (in my house), **da tua mala** (of your bag)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
